 we II 2°4l'S' 01-Wet and heavy. If the ground is cl-el)the Rocks (Buffs or Barred) will do !NO.&amp; -() Legliorns and Anconas give good the dryer ground the WYanniflot;notoit.: abaost ally breeds ea • 1--4t°llB L CampinCS, Sussex, "i egh°rns' n be kept- ftlel.. T TABLE BIRDS. 1'0,415-e 'birds form a separate branch, because 14tte"l.ug has somewhat more generous, (Indy ,C 1 be of tb (ill'eannot feed for eggs and table birds out Baltie. trough. Should the poultry-keeper otnelkist° develop this section of business hisof th 'll'-'lB May with advantage be crossed, and Pro: e!ottes giving best results, so far as flesh 146111" go, there is nothing to equal the good-4 (iarae—Dorking. 'This gives a bird of kelitisize And shape, carrying a lot of breast sros„Of a white colour and very juicy, and this oisl ierally reckoned as the premier table ':.,:n4llother heavy-fleshed cross is the Bork- --1„11/1 Orpington; this variety is generally titr3'lo,3--111 ja the prize lists at table fowl compe- 114d quickly fatten up. Other crosses kto• -"lan e —Buff Orpington, Orpington— /r3,41 (a favourite cross with the South Coun- avt4tt4lero), Faverolle—Buff Orpington, and ktilleralle,__lndian Game. There is a great de- that(l,2ll the early spring for table fowl, and l'elaunerative prices.</p>
        <p>Th, CHICKEN PRICES. 12 Prices , frequently obtained for chicks at old - run up to is. and is. 2d. per lb. '4tg,, fight. but do not try and get them too hitt% r the poultry dealer has a large call for thGe 203. to 31b., but if you get them over th Nice is getting too high, and there is qd.e ready sale for birds costing 4s. 6d. to that there is for 3s. to 3s. 9d. birds.</p>
