      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <head>LATCHFORD WEDD</head>
        <p>A LATCHFORD WEDD</p>
        <p>Marriage of Mr. Eric Fairclough Miss,. Janet Hutton.</p>
        <p>A pretty wedding took place at 6urcti, Latchford, on Saturday, the coat jug parties being Mr. Eric Fairclough, "13 field," Latchford, and Miss Janet Hutton, Grove," Latchford. The Rev. G. C. f! was the officiating clergyman, and Mr.' Fry, who presided at the organ, played oi priate wedding music.</p>
        <p>DRESSES.. Given away by her father, the bride 'charming in a beautiful gown of ivol</p>
        <p>eharmeu-se, trimmed. with point lace. TI was draped with pannier effect. The</p>
        <p>train, which WaS square, was prettily with chiffon, orange blossom and white and was caught at the left shoulder 4</p>
        <p>of embroidered Brussels net was worn wreath of orange blossom. • She carried of longilloriuna lilies, tied with broad satiti bons, the gift of the bridegroom. She was attended by three bridesnimiffkl Margaret Hutton (sister of the bride), Molly Fairclough (sister of the bridegroonl) ' Miss Newton—who wore beautiful dressef!, primrose satin charineuse. The bodices': trimmed with frills of old ivory-coloured I and the Skirts were prettily draped pannier style. They wore tete-de-negro 6t and tulle Watteau hats, with large Bali torian posies on and under the brim, still/ with moire ribbon, falling in a long boil the hair down the centre of the back. carried Early Victorian poses of primrose,' blue hyacinths to match the ones on the and wore long lace brooches set with pe° and pearls, the gifts of the bridegroom. The bride's mother was attired in an el!, reception gown of Andoise crepe meteor, tically draped skirt with charming ioatrodueti of irridescent and steel embroidery, and el to correspond. She wore a hat to matcli—t. ribbon toque, with flower crown in nie' shades, and large osprey coming from cenill flowers. She carried a bouquet of dark roses. iiree4</p>
        <p>The bride's travelling dress was a th. suit in tete-de-negre satin charmeuse:4ler to match was of tete-de-negre straw with brt Ospreys at the back, finished with Terry Mr. Egerton Fairclough was the best After the ceremony the newly-married 01/ left for London, and the honeymoon will be 611 there and on the South Coast. Spinal Failuri</p>
