      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0113" n="art0113">
        <head>Deaths.</head>
        <p>Deaths.</p>
        <p>TOWLINSON.—ApriI 19, at 141, Mersey-street, Thomas Henry Tomlinson, aged 39 years. AIORRELL.—ApriI 18, at 7, Goulden-street, Sarah Morrell, aged 76 years. HAYES.—ApriI 18, at 21, Ashton-street, John Hayes, aged 56 years. BROOKES.—ApriI 23, at 55, Tanner's-lane, Mar- garet Brookes, aged 47 years. MYLES.—ApriI 20, at 29, Rolleston-street, Mary Myles, aged 52 years. TAYLOR.—April 20, at 38, General-street, Samuel Taylor, aged 72 years. HOUGHTON.—On Thursday, April 23rd, at his residence, The Grange, Paddington. William Houghton, aged 68 years. Service to-day (Satur- day), Padgate Church, 1.45. Interment War- rington Cemetery, 2.30. Friends, please accept this, the only, intimation.</p>
        <p>In Memoriam. HARRIS.—In loving memory of Thomas Harris, who died April 25th, 1913. " They miss him most, who loved him best." HIS LOVING WIFE and CHILDREN. 199, Knutsford-road. JONES.—In loving memory of Thomas Jones, who died April 25th, 1913. HIS WIFE AND FAMILY. 2, Orford-avenue, Warrington.</p>
