        <p>NONA NOM NOM VOX Nal2lk VI" VIMk VI" NitS"</p>
        <p>:.wiet then as ir overcome ny tins apParc; admission of guilt, she grianed and le9 against the table for support. jill Ihere was a long pause, all three be*D deeply embarrassed. " You will lefive house, Mies Pallett ?" said Ilugh, brea the si:ence. el She started, and then looked appea:ilifi, at Christabel, who made no response ti 1,4 piteous appeal. And again silence fell tween them. tP It was broken this time by a knock at dcor, and Ruth turned quickly and bled. A servant entered, and handed parcel to Christabel. " These are what were asking about, miss, please." do! it was a box of chocolates, and hurjd her face iii her hands as Christai, took the box and hold it in trembling fi11,5, as she stared like one bereft of her her lover. •' Christabel!" he exclaimed, under breath in a tone of horror. Don't! Don't!" cried Ruth with all .1 vehemence, and shp snatched the box " They are mine. 'Mine, I say, not Cbtlite bel's. I swear they are mine, and I Vvc all you accused me of. I will go away, doc,„i I will, at once. Christabel, Uhristati?l, give way like this." But the appeal was to deaf ears. Chrigt•ltl, had fainted, and her lover, realising the.„, rib'e truth—that it was she and net who was guilty—turned away overwhe' and horrified by the discovery. 131 lie learnt the full truth a day or from a letter which Christabel herself him. She had been living a double life. e was already married, and being in dire !lye of money and imminent fear of disc'. I had fallen so low as to attempt to obtaig," aunt's fortune by slowly poisoning her. had disc wered the attempt and thwarteuff, and had held her tongue,. fearing the ; of the shock upon the woman who 111%;" 1 ways befriended her and confident 0' ability to protect her. Will you ever 'forgive me ?" asked of Ruth one day when the patient wag tient no longer but hale and strong ag, " I should have thought as you di"' replied with a sad smile. " I don't mean that, but for haviogkeri thought as I did about—about her _</p>
        <p>knew—" and he teak her hand. She left it in his. Thus through the dark clouds of tion the dawn of great and lasting 1131 broke for them both.</p>
      </div>
