        <p>Warrington played a great game in the second half, only they allowed chances to slip. Once five home forwards had the Rovers' line at their</p>
        <p>mercy. They made a bad mull of it and Smith was able to clear. -</p>
        <p>The Rovers were penalised for obstruction and Nicholas experienced hard lines in striking the cross-bar with the kick, the ball rebounding into, play and thiSs enabling Smith to clear. It looked as if Warrington would have to be content with a one-point lead, and it was only in the last 15 minutes that they were able to put the issue beyond doubt. Clare got possession, made a grand run, and scored. Nicholas got the 'goal points with ease, and the game ended: Warring- ton, 1 goal 3 tries (11 points); Hull Kingston Rovers, 1 goal 1 try (5 points).</p>
