      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0252" n="art0252">
        <head>HALF-BACKS' REVIVAL.</head>
        <p>HALF-BACKS' REVIVAL.</p>
        <p>_ ....._. The feature in the Warrington play was the marked revival in the play of the half-backs. The ground suited Nicholas and Young splen- didly, and thus they were able to show their style to the best advantage. Nicholas cleverly worked the scrums and made some smart indivi- dual runs.</p>
        <p>Young got the ball nicely away, ran and tackled smartly, and only was hampered by the slowness of the two centre threequarters. -Baker did well, and Waywell, although somewhat off colour, also gave a good account of himself. Dainteth was a good substitute for Jolley, and the forwards, with one exception, when they had the Hovers' line at disposal, were most reliable.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0253" n="art0253">
        <head>HYLANDS' FINE SEASON. Al on 21 Matches and Lost Three.</head>
        <p>HYLANDS' FINE SEASON. Al on 21 Matches and Lost Three.</p>
        <p>Rylands' have still two matches to play in order to wind up their season. They have been most successful, and out of the 27 matches have won 24 and only lost three. not, so far, lost a League match, thus 'all)dliaideyiyedng have other record to those they have already established. To-day they play Prestwich at lime. The following teams are to turn ?t,_</p>
        <p>Rylands'—F. Potter; J. Griffiths, F. Horrocks, A. Horrocks, and ,P. Morris; G. Warren and J. Gallop; A. Stretford (captain), J. Brandwood, H. Morris, D. Slater, J. Broadhurst, and H. Wel sby. The Prestwich team will be selected from the following : F. Hughes, D. Harrop, A. Kay, J. Thorpe, R. Callie, L. Barrett, R. Howcroft, H. Long, T. Wallington, J. Hocks, F. Ryder, J. Doyle, H. Foster, R. Morris, F. Howarth, G. Wilcox, and W. Murtha.</p>
        <p>Douglas, Indian, 8,5. A., Rudge and Sunbeam Motor Cycles</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0254" n="art0254">
        <head>FORD CARS</head>
        <p>FORD CARS</p>
        <p>Sole</p>
        <p>agent t W. KNIGHT, Stockton Heath Garage</p>
        <p>Garage for 16 Cars. Inspection Pits. Cars for Hire ONLY when Driven by Members of our own Staff.</p>
