      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0263" n="art0263">
        <head>AT THE LIBERAL CLUB.</head>
        <p>AT THE LIBERAL CLUB.</p>
        <p>The green adjoining the Liberal Club, in BeweeY-street, was, according to a large number who patronised it on Saturday, when the season commenced, in excellent condition. Some re- markably good bowling was witnessed, but the majority of the players, as can be imagined, were out of practice, and consequently there were but a few "touchers." The season here promises to be a most successful one; indeed, if .Saturday's turn-up can be regarded as a criterion, it should be a record year.</p>
        <p>CRICKET COMMENCED.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0264" n="art0264">
        <head>Warrington Club's Initial Win.</head>
        <p>Warrington Club's Initial Win.</p>
        <p>King Willow began hi s sway on Saturday. The weather was ideal for the opening of the cricket season, and the pitch was more favour- able to the 'batsman than to the bowler. it was a trifle fiery, and the bowlers had their work cut out, yet some good bowling feats were accomplished. Hannam, playing for Warrington first against Longsiglit, at Longsight, took five wickets at the cost of 23 runs. Be bowled 16 overs, four of which were maidens. B: Silcock even eclipsed this performance by taking four wickets at the cost of 16 runs. • Warrington won the match by 113 runs to 91. The top scorer was W. Richardson, who started the season splendidly by knocking up 52, the re- sult of good cricket. The details were : Longsight.—A. Fox b Hannam 0, A. Dunworth b Hannam 6, Ingleby b Hannam 7, C. S. Parker C Woodcock b Hannam 35, H. Ousey b Silcock 17, I. Higson b Partridge 4, A. W. Reynolds b Silcock 8, G. Beeson lbw b Silcock 0, G. A. McCubbin not out 5, F. Grattridge b Hannam 1, E. M. Broadie b Silcock Of extras 8; total 91. Warrington.—B. Silcock b Ingleby 0, Cr. Wood- cock b Ingleby 0, S.• Partridge b Ingleby 0, W. Richardson b Ingleby 52, J. Bradburn b Broadie 8, Hannam c Ingleby b Grattridge 12, H. Haw- thorn run out 14, S. Baxter b Broadie 14, T. Burns not out 2, W. Bennett c Grattridge b FOX 4, A. Duckworth b Broadie 0; extras 7; total 113.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON 2nd V. LONGSIGHT 2nd.</p>
        <p>..... Played at Warrington. Scores : Warrington.—J. Thompson lbw 'b Warnes 10, IL Evans c Cattrall b Dibb 12, W. Howard c Robinson b Warnes 8, W. V. Turton b Dibb 2, W. H. Bell b Dibb 1, W. Mclntyre not out 3, Whitlow b Dibb 1, F. Tole c Meakin h Dibb 2, P. Lemon c Cattrall b Dibb 1, J. Stirrup c Warnes b Dibb 6, E. White lbw b Dibb 6; extras 5; total 51. Longsight.—H. Robinson c Bell b White 8, C. Hewitt c Turton b Evans 8, W. Warnes b Bell 6, F. Latham c Tole b Evans 10, H. Gibson c Evans b Howard 6, A. F. Miniatti c Bell b Lemon 4, H. W. Cattrall run out 3. W. H. Lynas b Lemon 9, E. Dibb b Howard 4, J. Meakin not out 1, Taylor c Whitlow 1) Lemon 2; extras 7; total 69.</p>
      </div>
