      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-04-25_WidnesExaminer_art0301" n="art0301">
        <p>PUBLIC AMUSEMENTS</p>
        <p>"THE KELLY GANG" 'NEXT WEE Those who like plenty of fan and excite will find it next week at the Royal I Theatre, where The Kelly aang" will b( seated for the first time in Warrington. drama deals with different incidents OS supposed to have occurred during the Ii Ned Kelly, the notorious bushranger, who, his accomplices, got into many a tight cc but always managed to get out again till the help of Kelly's sister Kate. Kelly's from a house while the police are searcliV his escape from his hut and from Ballarat are a few of the exciting situations, whiel minate in Kelly and his "mates" holdir the Glenrowan Inn, to which the police se The story is a powerful one, with many tli.r episodes, and a strong dramatic interest tamed all through the. play, which is pleas relieved here and there( with comedy elenLn</p>
        <p>"THE KITCHEN SMILE." "Bungle!, Luck" at Hippodrome A bright, breezy and attractive-snow* seen at the Hippodrome this week, where' Kitchen and his own company, who heal bill, are delighting large audiences night "Bungle's Luck." Kitchen sends the aud into uncontrollable fits of mirth as Bunglo escaped convict, who has such a lively el ence in society. His drollery, burlesque col and eccentric make-ups are perfect, and safe to say that we have not had such a wholesome comedy at the Hippodrome for time. Mr. Kitchen is ably supported by M Tom Kayne, L. Benson, J. E. Coyle, F. Pa Ernest Weste, Philip Sinclair, John osl H. Piddock, Miss Marie Fontaine and Aggie Morris. Numerous diverting specii are introduced, including the "Ragtime I man."</p>
        <p>Daring is not a sufficiently adequate NrC describe the cycle turn given by the Ira: Cycle Troupe, for they perform the most vellous tricks in such a rapid manner. A feature is the aerial football match, and are the " hairsbreadtli " escapes by the formers. The Phydoras introduce sonic entirely new to us in their eccentric da and musical novelty act, in the way of •sa staircase. Mabel and Cliff Diamond d with their cleFer singing and dancing particularly with the "Dutch" number. Clifford is a character comedian, who, style of his own, cannot fail to please.</p>
        <p>Amstell is also a smart eccentric comedie Godfrey assisted by Miss Vedo, gives a ample of his dexterity as a comedy card rag lator.</p>
        <p>Great Attractions Next Week.</p>
        <p>Another large number of talented artiste pay their first visit to the Hippodrome week, and these include Bowdon and St comedy jumping act; Naughton and Gold, dians; Harry Rignold, supported by Miss Shine and Mr. Drew Mackintosh, in a playlet, "Fido," the bulldog detective; Dancing Middies, in novel dancing act; " Zaza," the Argentine wonder; The Br Obo, laughing comedians; Nellie Bly, Girl in the Frame"; and a return visit 14 paid by The Bouncing Dillons, novelty nasts.</p>
      </div>
